WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.536
[dramatic music]

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.771
We are here to
document the lives

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.206
of people living in Alaska.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.274
The harsh reality is the
environment we're up against.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.376
It makes it tough to do our job.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.610
Get out of there!

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.946
Working on "Life Below
Zero" can be very dangerous.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.080
Guns here.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:14.981
Cameras here.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:15.915
Never know what to expect.
Hey!

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:16.750
Hey!

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.017
You [bleep] see that [bleep]?

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.720
It's gonna be tough, but
we're gonna get the shot.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.223
Every scenario, we
gotta prepare for this.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.424
But we're still smiling.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.425
We're having fun.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.228
We're still making
"Life Below Zero."

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.329
Yes!

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.130
Bring it on.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:33.566
[suspenseful music]

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:46.279
It's 9:00 AM, day five
of our extended stay

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.481
here at Chandalar.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.885
Still waiting for a weather
window to get a plane in here.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.654
It's beautiful blue
sky here, but the area

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.791
in between here and where we
need to get to is the problem.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:00.260
We're wrapped,
but here we remain.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.830
It's 13 days without
plumbing or heat.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.799
Every day I thought--
including today--

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.134
I thought there was a really
good chance we would get out.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:11.971
Messaging back and forth
via satellite to the office,

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.640
and they're doing our best--

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.009
their best to keep us
safe, so I appreciate that.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.344
And we just gotta wait until
things are safe to get out.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.512
What can you do?

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.080
Man makes plans and God laughs.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.589
So this is our
gear pile staged

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.459
on the beach ready to
go if we get the call

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.693
that the plane is coming in.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.828
We're just going
to leave this out

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.796
unless the weather
gets really bad.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.665
We've run pretty low on food.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:42.101
It's definitely getting to the
point where we're scraping by.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.737
Some peanut butter, this
could come in handy.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.907
A couple of cans of sardines.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.209
That's about it.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.912
Probably at about two or
three days of food left.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.420
We moved into Glen's sod house.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.356
It's got an open door and
then a hole in the roof.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:06.359
Dragged our tarp over here
to kind of close up the roof

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:09.429
hole a little bit to keep
a bit more of the heat in.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.397
We'd set up cots
that just barely

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.032
fit in the open space in there.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.235
And it's been a pretty
great little home.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:20.573
So here's our door to
keep the heat in at night.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.876
It takes a little
bit of gymnastics

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.644
to get out in the
middle of the night

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.247
without making a lot of noise
and waking up your mates,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.882
but it keeps the
heat in really well.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.256
We need some wood to
keep our sod house warm.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.025
We don't want to burn
all of Glen's wood,

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:43.363
so we're going to go out
into the forest and get some.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.466
It'll keep us warm later, and
it'll warm us up right now

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.735
and give us something to do.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.937
Well, you want a
standing dead tree,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.639
so you're looking
for one that doesn't

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:55.875
have any green needles on it.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.311
It doesn't seem like
it's green at all.

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:59.879
It seems like it's dead.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.481
We could try for that one.

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:02.882
I think we could take that down.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.551
I think it'd be fun.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.987
[dramatic music]

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.030
Guy's a human beaver.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.539
Starting to have
a little concern

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.374
about it falling the other way.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.710
We'll see what happens.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.079
Yeah, I think it wants
to go the other way.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.447
It's almost ready to go, Tony.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.352
Get out of there!

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:42.255
[crashing]

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.725
Yeah!

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.027
We got firewood.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.697
So now that we've dropped
this tree on the ground,

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:54.801
we need to cut it up
into manageable pieces.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:58.538
We're about a quarter mile
from the sod house right here,

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:01.274
so we're going to have to just
carry them on our shoulders.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.842
We don't want to
cut them too big,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.844
but we don't want to cut
them too small because that

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.947
means more cuts and more trips.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.717
So we'll just take a guess
at what the right length is

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.319
and cut it up into some chunks.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.728
Warm you up for sure.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.129
You know what they say, Tony.

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.130
Wood warms you twice.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:31.404
We've got the tree cut up
into four usable chunks

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:35.341
that I think we can manage to
carry out of here on our own.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.609
So we'll do two trips.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.912
We'll throw them up on our
shoulders, walk them out.

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.854
[dramatic music]

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:02.535
Good job.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.336
That was fun.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:04.137
Yeah, it was.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.738
Thank you.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:08.174
[birds hooting]

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:10.376
All right.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:13.546
This should do us for the while.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.214
Thanks for getting
all that wood, Natch.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.783
Yeah, that was a fun project.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:17.917
Yeah.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:18.851
Good group effort.

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:25.858
It's getting colder every
night, and having all this wood

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.227
is a killer thing to do.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.496
I mean, not only is it, like--

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:33.099
it's keeping us warm in here,
for one thing, for sure.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:36.169
But just having something to
do, just trapped in this sort

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:39.806
of weird limbo that
we're in waiting,

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:42.642
waiting, waiting for a new
message from production,

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:45.344
a new message from
our friends or family,

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.046
and just trying to
find something to do

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.383
in the meantime to fill time.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.051
One of my favorite
things about spending

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:54.921
an extended period of time
out in the backcountry

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.923
is it really gives
you an appreciation

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.759
for all the things that we
can kind of take for granted.

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:01.828
Food is a huge part
of that for the crew.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.497
I'm very, very excited.

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:05.465
It smells amazing.

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.801
[soft music]

